## Changelog Format for Future Entries

Each subsequent entry should follow this structure:

```
## v[X.X] — [DATE] — [Brief description of what changed]

### What changed
[List of specific skills or sections updated]

### Why it changed
[The feedback signal or reasoning that drove the change — link to debrief week if applicable]

### What was tested before the change
[Brief note on what the previous version was doing and why it wasn't working]

### Impact on testers
[Whether existing testers need to update their project instructions and how to notify them]
```

---

## How Version Numbers Work

**Minor updates (v1.0 → v1.1)** — Single skill tightened, one framework added to the reference library, a guardrail added or removed, a stress test reworded. Testers should update but the change is not disruptive.

**Significant updates (v1.0 → v2.0)** — A skill substantially rewritten, a new skill added to the chain, the reference library expanded with a new thinker, or a structural change to how the chain operates. Testers must update. A note explaining the change and its implications should accompany the release.
